{"uid":"8e884d4a69c35d84","name":"test_terminal_event_on_disk_with_status_json_still_running_needs_the_new_barrier","fullName":"tests.flows.test_flowlib_status_barrier#test_terminal_event_on_disk_with_status_json_still_running_needs_the_new_barrier","historyId":"01fb58da70c77bac0505f6c16d61c710","time":{"start":1791925986498,"stop":1791925986664,"duration":166},"description":"Drives a run dir whose ending `state` event is already on disk while\n    `status.json` still reads `running` -- exactly the ordering the events\n    barrier alone permits, and exactly what the nightly run hit. Without\n    `wait_status_terminal`, the only thing a caller could do after the\n    events barrier returns is read `status.json` directly off disk, which\n    this asserts still reads the pre-terminal state at that moment -- i.e.\n    this scenario fails an \"it must be succeeded now\" assertion without the\n    new barrier. `wait_status_terminal` then bridges the remaining gap and\n    returns the terminal status once the second write actually lands.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Drives a run dir whose ending <code>state</code> event is already on disk while<br />\n<code>status.json</code> still reads <code>running</code> -- exactly the ordering the events<br />\nbarrier alone permits, and exactly what the nightly run hit. Without<br />\n<code>wait_status_terminal</code>, the only thing a caller could do after the<br />\nevents barrier returns is read <code>status.json</code> directly off disk, which<br />\nthis asserts still reads the pre-terminal state at that moment -- i.e.<br />\nthis scenario fails an &quot;it must be succeeded now&quot; assertion without the<br />\nnew barrier. <code>wait_status_terminal</code> then bridges the remaining gap and<br />\nreturns the terminal status once the second write actually lands.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"eve